---
name: encounter
description: >
  First-person memory of noticing another resident mid-activity (issue #370):
  the cheap perceive pass writes one of these into each mid-activity agent's
  stream when another resident newly comes within mutual sight, so a
  passed-by face is remembered even though no decision point fired. Rendered
  by cognition.maybe_react(); only reachable when the react gate
  (CognitionConfig.react_enabled) is on, so the default replay is
  byte-identical.
inputs:
  partner:
    type: string
    description: The name of the resident who came into view.
  doing:
    type: string
    description: >
      What this agent was doing at the time -- "walking to <place>" mid-walk,
      or its current activity while performing.
sample:
  partner: Ayesha Khan
  doing: walking to Van Pelt Library
---
I noticed {{ partner }} nearby while {{ doing }}.
